  "Comment": "CloudLab c240g5, Wikipedia: task migration (E6) as fetch on demand + drain, at 90 s: every partition of n4 goes to n5, a node that joins, by a placement plan (the one the Migrate runs carry out: n1-n3 keep theirs), under lazy with FetchExtra 0. n4 leaves the placement as in a scale-in, so after the flip the drain moves every raw vector only n4 holds to n5 (RAW_HELD_BY, RAW_PULL: unpaced, written through n5's page cache) while queries fetch what they need on demand; the rescale returns once n4 is drained, and n4 is offline. The load stays at the 4 -> 8 runs' first rate, 560 q/s (0.6 x C4 938, 2026-11-20), for 1200 s, as in the other migrate runs.",
